(function(E){ const x = E["hr-m6"] = E["hr-m6"] || {units:{}}; x.units["hr-6-3"] = {"explain":{"id":"c-hr-6-3-e","course":"hr","unit":"hr-6-3","type":"explain","level":"B1","title":{"en":"Meetings and HR data","tr":"Toplantılar ve İK verileri","fa":"جلسه‌ها و داده‌های منابع انسانی"},"objective":{"en":"After this lesson, you can lead a short meeting and present simple HR data with clear trend words.","tr":"Bu dersin sonunda kısa bir toplantıyı yönetip basit İK verilerini net eğilim ifadeleriyle sunabileceksin.","fa":"بعد از این درس می‌توانی یک جلسه‌ی کوتاه را اداره کنی و داده‌های ساده‌ی منابع انسانی را با کلمه‌های روشن برای روندها توضیح بدهی."},"hook":{"en":"Say what each number means. Leaders act on your numbers only when they understand and trust them. Ms Clarke says 'That's interesting' when she doubts you. Clear trend words, and one definition, won her trust.","tr":"Her sayının ne anlama geldiğini söyle. Yöneticiler sayılarına ancak onları anlayıp güvendiklerinde göre hareket eder. Ms Clarke şüphelendiğinde 'That's interesting' der. Net eğilim kelimeleri ve tek bir tanım onun güvenini kazandı.","fa":"بگو هر عدد یعنی چه. مدیرها فقط وقتی بر اساس عددهای تو عمل می‌کنند که آن‌ها را بفهمند و به آن‌ها اعتماد کنند. خانم کلارک وقتی شک دارد می‌گوید «That's interesting». کلمه‌های روشن برای روندها و یک تعریف ساده اعتمادش را جلب کرد."},"before":{"en":"Write two sentences about HR figures for a client: what moved, by how much, and what one term means.","tr":"Bir müşteri için İK rakamları hakkında iki cümle yaz: ne değişti, ne kadar ve bir terimin anlamı ne.","fa":"برای یک مشتری درباره‌ی آمار منابع انسانی دو جمله بنویس: چه چیزی تغییر کرد، چقدر و یک اصطلاح چه معنایی دارد."},"rounds":[[1,4],[2,3]],"stats":[{"label":{"en":"Key points","tr":"Ana nokta","fa":"نکته‌ی اصلی"},"value":"4"},{"label":{"en":"Key phrases","tr":"Anahtar ifade","fa":"عبارت کلیدی"},"value":"5"},{"label":{"en":"Practice tasks","tr":"Alıştırma","fa":"تمرین"},"value":"4"}],"points":[{"eyebrow":{"en":"The skill","tr":"Beceri","fa":"مهارت"},"head":{"en":"Say what the number means","tr":"Sayının ne anlama geldiğini söyle","fa":"بگو این عدد یعنی چه"},"body":{"en":"A chart alone makes no point. Say what moved, by how much and what it means. Define any term people might read differently. In a meeting, give the agenda and the finish time first.","tr":"Tek başına bir grafik bir şey anlatmaz. Neyin, ne kadar değiştiğini ve bunun ne anlama geldiğini söyle. Farklı anlaşılabilecek her terimi tanımla. Toplantıda önce gündemi ve bitiş saatini söyle.","fa":"نمودار به‌تنهایی چیزی نمی‌گوید. بگو چه چیزی، چقدر تغییر کرده و این یعنی چه. هر اصطلاحی را که ممکن است جور دیگری فهمیده شود تعریف کن. در جلسه، اول دستور جلسه و ساعت پایان را بگو."}},{"eyebrow":{"en":"The language","tr":"Dil","fa":"زبان"},"head":{"en":"Describing trends: rose sharply, levelled off; moving on to...","tr":"Eğilimleri anlatmak: rose sharply, levelled off; moving on to...","fa":"توصیف روند: rose sharply، levelled off؛ moving on to..."},"steps":[{"en":"Up: rise, increase. Down: fall, drop. Flat: level off. Top: peak.","tr":"Yukarı: rise, increase. Aşağı: fall, drop. Sabit: level off. Zirve: peak.","fa":"برای بالا رفتن rise و increase، برای پایین آمدن fall و drop، برای ثابت ماندن level off و برای رسیدن به اوج peak را به کار ببر.","ex":"Turnover rose sharply in July, then levelled off."},{"en":"Add an adverb for size and speed.","tr":"Büyüklük ve hız için bir zarf ekle.","fa":"برای اندازه و سرعت یک قید اضافه کن.","ex":"sharply, slightly, steadily"},{"en":"Numbers rise; people raise things.","tr":"Sayılar rise eder; insanlar bir şeyi raise eder.","fa":"عددها rise می‌کنند؛ آدم‌ها چیزی را raise می‌کنند.","ex":"Turnover rose. We raised salaries."},{"en":"Signpost each new topic.","tr":"Her yeni konuyu işaretle.","fa":"هر موضوع تازه را اعلام کن.","ex":"Let's move on to retention."}],"table":{"headers":{"en":["Movement","Verb (past)","Example"],"tr":["Hareket","Fiil (geçmiş)","Örnek"],"fa":["حرکت","فعل (شکل گذشته)","مثال"]},"rows":[["Up","rose / increased","Turnover rose sharply in July."],["Down","fell / dropped","Late deliveries fell from 9% to 3%."],["No change","levelled off","It levelled off at one leaver a month."],["Topic change","Let's move on to...","Let's move on to retention."]]},"tip":{"en":"Turkish artmak / artırmak and Persian bala raftan / bala bordan split this the same way as rise / raise. Use that to choose.","tr":"Türkçedeki artmak / artırmak ayrımı rise / raise ile aynıdır: turnover arttı (rose), maaşları artırdık (raised).","fa":"در فارسی «بالا رفتن» و «بالا بردن» دقیقاً همین تفاوت rise و raise را دارند: نرخ ترک خدمت بالا رفت (rose)، حقوق‌ها را بالا بردیم (raised)."},"wrong":"Turnover raised sharply in July.","right":"Turnover rose sharply in July."},{"eyebrow":{"en":"Key phrases","tr":"Anahtar ifadeler","fa":"عبارت‌های کلیدی"},"head":{"en":"Phrases for this task","tr":"Bu görev için ifadeler","fa":"عبارت‌های این کار"},"phrases":[{"phrase":"We have three items on the agenda.","meaning":{"en":"Opens the meeting.","tr":"Toplantıyı açar.","fa":"جلسه را شروع می‌کند."}},{"phrase":"Let's move on to...","meaning":{"en":"Changes topic.","tr":"Konuyu değiştirir.","fa":"به موضوع بعدی می‌رود."}},{"phrase":"Let me define..., so we read it the same way.","meaning":{"en":"Builds trust in the numbers.","tr":"Sayılara güven oluşturur.","fa":"اعتماد به عددها را بیشتر می‌کند."}},{"phrase":"retention","meaning":{"en":"Keeping employees; the share who stay.","tr":"çalışanı elde tutma.","fa":"نگهداشت کارکنان (درصد کسانی که می‌مانند)"}},{"phrase":"headcount","meaning":{"en":"The number of people employed.","tr":"çalışan sayısı.","fa":"تعداد کارکنان؛ تعداد نیرو"}}]},{"eyebrow":{"en":"At work","tr":"İş yerinde","fa":"در محیط کار"},"head":{"en":"Hear the polite doubt","tr":"Kibar şüpheyi duy","fa":"تردیدِ مؤدبانه را بشنو"},"body":{"en":"Many British speakers use mild words to show doubt or disagreement. \"That's interesting\" or \"I hear what you say\" can mean \"I'm not convinced\". \"With respect\" often comes before a disagreement. When you hear them, slow down and give a definition, a source or an example.","tr":"Birçok İngiliz şüphe ya da itirazı göstermek için yumuşak sözcükler kullanır. \"That's interesting\" ya da \"I hear what you say\" \"ikna olmadım\" anlamına gelebilir. \"With respect\" çoğu zaman bir itirazdan önce gelir. Bunları duyduğunda yavaşla ve bir tanım, kaynak ya da örnek ver.","fa":"بسیاری از بریتانیایی‌ها تردید یا مخالفتشان را با کلمه‌های ملایم نشان می‌دهند. «That's interesting» یا «I hear what you say» ممکن است در واقع یعنی «قانع نشدم». «With respect» هم اغلب درست قبل از یک مخالفت می‌آید. وقتی این عبارت‌ها را می‌شنوی، آهسته‌تر پیش برو و یک تعریف، یک منبع یا یک مثال بیاور."}}],"example":{"eyebrow":{"en":"Worked example","tr":"Çözümlü örnek","fa":"مثال حل‌شده"},"head":{"en":"From weak to strong","tr":"Zayıftan güçlüye","fa":"از عدد خالی تا عدد با معنی"},"text":"Facts: Turnover reached 14% in June, when five staff left. Definition: leavers divided by average headcount.","item":"Turnover is 14%. Next slide.","why":{"en":"Weak: a number with no meaning. Strong: the movement, the cause and a definition.","tr":"Zayıf: anlamı olmayan bir sayı. Güçlü: değişim, neden ve bir tanım.","fa":"نسخه‌ی اول عددی است بدون معنی. نسخه‌ی دوم تغییر، دلیل و یک تعریف دارد."},"answer":"Turnover rose to 14% in June, when five staff left. We count leavers divided by average headcount.","cut":["Next slide."],"cutHint":{"en":"Tap what moves on before saying what the number means.","tr":"Rakamın ne anlama geldiğini söylemeden geçen kısma dokun.","fa":"روی بخشی بزن که قبل از گفتن معنای عدد، از آن رد می‌شود."}},"quick":{"prompt":"You open an HR data review with a client. What do you say first?","options":["The agenda and the finish time","The most worrying number","A joke to relax everyone"],"correct":0,"why":{"en":"The agenda and the finish time: then people know what is coming and can follow each number.","tr":"Gündem ve bitiş saati: Böylece insanlar neyin geleceğini bilir ve her rakamı takip edebilir.","fa":"دستور جلسه و ساعت پایان: این‌طوری همه می‌دانند چه چیزی در پیش است و می‌توانند هر عدد را دنبال کنند."},"point":1},"remember":{"en":"Is there an object after the verb (raised salaries)? raise. No object (turnover rose)? rise. Result of this lesson: you can lead a short meeting and explain HR data. You also have a follow-up email.","tr":"Fiilden sonra nesne var mı (raised salaries)? raise. Nesne yok mu (turnover rose)? rise. Bu dersin sonucu: kısa bir toplantıyı yönetip İK verilerini açıklayabilirsin ve elinde bir takip e-postası olur.","fa":"بعد از فعل مفعول هست (raised salaries)؟ raise. مفعول نیست (turnover rose)؟ ⁨rise⁩. حالا می‌توانی جلسه‌ای کوتاه را اداره کنی و داده‌های منابع انسانی را توضیح بدهی. ایمیل پیگیری هم آماده است."},"b2Point":{"eyebrow":{"en":"B2 track","tr":"B2 yolu","fa":"مسیر B2"},"head":{"en":"Highlighting with wh-clefts: What stands out is...","tr":"Wh-cleft ile vurgulamak: What stands out is...","fa":"برجسته‌سازی با wh-cleft: What stands out is..."},"steps":[{"en":"What + clause + is/was + the key point.","tr":"What + yan cümle + is/was + asıl nokta.","fa":"الگو این است: What و یک جمله، بعد is یا was و بعد نکته‌ی اصلی.","ex":"What surprised us was the July peak."},{"en":"No it before is.","tr":"is'ten önce it yok.","fa":"پیش از is کلمه‌ی it نمی‌آید.","ex":"What stands out is..., not What stands out it is..."},{"en":"Not 'the thing what': use what alone or the thing that.","tr":"'the thing what' değil: yalnızca what ya da the thing that.","fa":"«the thing what» نه؛ فقط what یا ⁨the thing that⁩.","ex":"What we need to understand is why people leave in summer."}],"table":{"headers":{"en":["Plain","Wh-cleft"],"tr":["Düz","Wh-cleft"],"fa":["جمله‌ی ساده","wh-cleft"]},"rows":[["The drop in late deliveries stands out.","What stands out is the drop in late deliveries."],["The July peak surprised us.","What surprised us was the July peak."],["We need to understand why people leave.","What we need to understand is why people leave."]]},"body":{"en":"B2 track: use two wh-clefts in your presentation: one to highlight good news, one to name the open question.","tr":"B2 yolu: sunumunda iki wh-cleft kullan: biri iyi haberi vurgulamak, biri açık soruyu belirtmek için.","fa":"مسیر B2: در ارائه‌ات دو wh-cleft به کار ببر: یکی برای برجسته کردن خبر خوب و یکی برای مطرح کردن پرسشی که هنوز بی‌جواب مانده است."}}},"grammar":{"id":"c-hr-6-3-g","level":"B1","course":"hr","unit":"hr-6-3","title":"Describing trends: rose sharply, levelled off; moving on to...","titleTr":"Eğilimleri anlatmak: rose sharply, levelled off; moving on to...","exp":{"en":"Data talk uses a small set of verbs plus adverbs. Up: rise (rose, risen), increase, go up. Down: fall (fell, fallen), drop, go down. No change: level off, stay the same. Highest point: peak. Add an adverb for size and speed: sharply, slightly, steadily. \"Turnover rose sharply in July, then levelled off.\" Two traps. Rise is irregular: \"rose\", never \"rised\". And raise is different: it needs an object (\"We raised salaries\"), so numbers rise, people raise things: not \"turnover raised\". To lead the meeting, signpost each change of topic: \"Let's move on to retention.\", \"Moving on to the next item...\".","tr":"Veri konuşması az sayıda fiil ve zarf kullanır. Artış: rise (rose, risen), increase, go up. Azalış: fall (fell, fallen), drop, go down. Değişim yok: level off, stay the same. En yüksek nokta: peak. Büyüklük ve hız için zarf ekle: sharply, slightly, steadily. \"Turnover rose sharply in July, then levelled off.\" İki tuzak var. Rise düzensizdir: \"rose\", asla \"rised\" değil. Raise ise farklıdır: bir nesne ister (\"We raised salaries\"); yani sayılar rise eder, insanlar bir şeyi raise eder: \"turnover raised\" değil. Toplantıyı yönetmek için her konu değişimini işaretle: \"Let's move on to retention.\", \"Moving on to the next item...\".","fa":"برای حرف زدن درباره‌ی داده‌ها فقط چند فعل و قید لازم داری. افزایش: rise (rose، risen)، increase و go up. کاهش: fall (fell، fallen)، drop و go down. بدون تغییر: level off و stay the same. بالاترین نقطه: peak. برای نشان دادن اندازه و سرعتِ تغییر، یک قید اضافه کن: sharply (شدید)، slightly (جزئی)، steadily (پیوسته). «⁨Turnover rose sharply in July, then levelled off.⁩» دو تله در کار است. rise بی‌قاعده است: «rose»، هرگز «rised». و raise فعل دیگری است که مفعول می‌خواهد («We raised salaries»)؛ یعنی عددها خودشان rise می‌کنند و آدم‌ها چیزی را raise می‌کنند، پس «turnover raised» غلط است؛ درست مثل فرق «بالا رفتن» و «بالا بردن» در فارسی. برای اداره‌ی جلسه، هر بار که موضوع عوض می‌شود آن را اعلام کن: «⁨Let's move on to retention.⁩» یا «⁨Moving on to the next item...⁩»."},"formsTable":{"headers":{"en":["Movement","Verb (past)","Example"],"tr":["Hareket","Fiil (geçmiş)","Örnek"],"fa":["حرکت","فعل (شکل گذشته)","مثال"]},"rows":[["Up","rose / increased","Turnover rose sharply in July."],["Down","fell / dropped","Late deliveries fell from 9% to 3%."],["No change","levelled off","It levelled off at one leaver a month."],["Topic change","Let's move on to...","Let's move on to retention."]]},"wrong":"Turnover raised sharply in July.","right":"Turnover rose sharply in July.","blank":{"sentence":"Turnover ___ sharply in July.","word":"rose","distractors":["rised","raised"]},"wrong2":"Late deliveries have fell to 3%.","right2":"Late deliveries have fallen to 3%.","blank2":{"sentence":"Let's move ___ to retention.","word":"on","distractors":["in","at"]},"expParts":{"tryFrom":"blank","hook":{"en":"Ms Clarke says 'That's interesting' when she doubts you. Clear trend words, and one definition, won her trust.","tr":"Ms Clarke şüphelendiğinde 'That's interesting' der. Net eğilim kelimeleri ve tek bir tanım onun güvenini kazandı.","fa":"خانم کلارک وقتی شک دارد می‌گوید «That's interesting». کلمه‌های روشن برای روندها و یک تعریف ساده اعتمادش را جلب کرد."},"tryWhy":{"en":"rose: rise is irregular (rise, rose, risen). 'rised' does not exist, and raise needs an object.","tr":"rose: rise düzensizdir (rise, rose, risen). 'rised' diye bir şey yok; raise ise nesne ister.","fa":"جواب rose است: فعل rise بی‌قاعده است (rise، rose، risen). rised وجود ندارد و raise مفعول می‌خواهد."},"rule":[{"en":"Up: rise, increase. Down: fall, drop. Flat: level off. Top: peak.","tr":"Yukarı: rise, increase. Aşağı: fall, drop. Sabit: level off. Zirve: peak.","fa":"برای بالا رفتن rise و increase، برای پایین آمدن fall و drop، برای ثابت ماندن level off و برای رسیدن به اوج peak را به کار ببر.","ex":"Turnover rose sharply in July, then levelled off."},{"en":"Add an adverb for size and speed.","tr":"Büyüklük ve hız için bir zarf ekle.","fa":"برای اندازه و سرعت یک قید اضافه کن.","ex":"sharply, slightly, steadily"},{"en":"Numbers rise; people raise things.","tr":"Sayılar rise eder; insanlar bir şeyi raise eder.","fa":"عددها rise می‌کنند؛ آدم‌ها چیزی را raise می‌کنند.","ex":"Turnover rose. We raised salaries."},{"en":"Signpost each new topic.","tr":"Her yeni konuyu işaretle.","fa":"هر موضوع تازه را اعلام کن.","ex":"Let's move on to retention."}],"test":{"en":"Is there an object after the verb (raised salaries)? raise. No object (turnover rose)? rise.","tr":"Fiilden sonra nesne var mı (raised salaries)? raise. Nesne yok mu (turnover rose)? rise.","fa":"بعد از فعل مفعول هست (raised salaries)؟ raise. مفعول نیست (turnover rose)؟ ⁨rise⁩."},"contrast":{"en":"Turkish artmak / artırmak and Persian bala raftan / bala bordan split this the same way as rise / raise. Use that to choose.","tr":"Türkçedeki artmak / artırmak ayrımı rise / raise ile aynıdır: turnover arttı (rose), maaşları artırdık (raised).","fa":"در فارسی «بالا رفتن» و «بالا بردن» دقیقاً همین تفاوت rise و raise را دارند: نرخ ترک خدمت بالا رفت (rose)، حقوق‌ها را بالا بردیم (raised)."}},"errorWatch":[{"find":["rised","turnover raised","deliveries raised","numbers raised","headcount raised"],"fix":{"en":"Numbers rise (rose, risen); people raise things: 'Turnover rose sharply.'","tr":"Sayılar rise eder (rose, risen); insanlar bir şeyi raise eder: 'Turnover rose sharply.'","fa":"عددها rise می‌کنند (rose، risen)؛ آدم‌ها چیزی را raise می‌کنند: «⁨Turnover rose sharply.⁩»"}},{"find":["have fell","has fell","have rose","has rose","have drop"],"fix":{"en":"After have / has use the past participle: fallen, risen, dropped.","tr":"have / has'ten sonra past participle kullan: fallen, risen, dropped.","fa":"بعد از have یا has اسم مفعول بیاور: fallen، risen، ⁨dropped⁩."}}]},"b2":{"id":"c-hr-6-3-b2","level":"B2","track":"B2","course":"hr","unit":"hr-6-3","title":"Highlighting with wh-clefts: What stands out is...","titleTr":"Wh-cleft ile vurgulamak: What stands out is...","exp":{"en":"A wh-cleft moves the key point to the end of the sentence, where listeners pay most attention: \"What stands out is the drop in late deliveries.\", \"What surprised us was the July peak.\", \"What we need to understand is why people leave in summer.\" The pattern is What + clause + be + the focus. It is excellent for presentations because it tells the audience \"listen, this is the important part\". Traps: do not add it (\"What stands out it is\"), and do not write \"the thing what\" (use \"the thing that\" or just \"what\").","tr":"Wh-cleft yapısı ana noktayı, dinleyenlerin en çok dikkat ettiği cümle sonuna taşır: \"What stands out is the drop in late deliveries.\", \"What surprised us was the July peak.\", \"What we need to understand is why people leave in summer.\" Kalıp: What + yan cümle + be + odak. Sunumlar için mükemmeldir, çünkü dinleyicilere \"dinleyin, önemli kısım bu\" der. Tuzaklar: araya it ekleme (\"What stands out it is\") ve \"the thing what\" yazma (\"the thing that\" ya da sadece \"what\" kullan).","fa":"ساختار wh-cleft نکته‌ی اصلی را به آخر جمله می‌برد؛ همان جایی که شنونده بیشترین توجه را دارد: «⁨What stands out is the drop in late deliveries.⁩»، «⁨What surprised us was the July peak.⁩» و «⁨What we need to understand is why people leave in summer.⁩» در فارسی هم همین کار را می‌کنیم: «چیزی که جلب توجه می‌کند، کاهش تأخیرهاست». الگو: what + جمله + فعل be + نکته‌ی اصلی. برای ارائه فوق‌العاده است، چون به مخاطب علامت می‌دهد که «حالا گوش کنید، بخش مهم این است». دو تله: it اضافه نکن (نه «What stands out it is»)، و ننویس «the thing what» (بگو «the thing that» یا فقط «what»)."},"formsTable":{"headers":{"en":["Plain","Wh-cleft"],"tr":["Düz","Wh-cleft"],"fa":["جمله‌ی ساده","wh-cleft"]},"rows":[["The drop in late deliveries stands out.","What stands out is the drop in late deliveries."],["The July peak surprised us.","What surprised us was the July peak."],["We need to understand why people leave.","What we need to understand is why people leave."]]},"wrong":"What stands out it is the drop in late deliveries.","right":"What stands out is the drop in late deliveries.","blank":{"sentence":"___ stands out is the drop in late deliveries.","word":"What","distractors":["That","It"]},"wrong2":"The thing what surprised us is the July peak.","right2":"What surprised us is the July peak.","blank2":{"sentence":"What we need to understand ___ why people leave in July.","word":"is","distractors":["are","that"]},"useIn":{"en":"B2 track: use two wh-clefts in your presentation: one to highlight good news, one to name the open question.","tr":"B2 yolu: sunumunda iki wh-cleft kullan: biri iyi haberi vurgulamak, biri açık soruyu belirtmek için.","fa":"مسیر B2: در ارائه‌ات دو wh-cleft به کار ببر: یکی برای برجسته کردن خبر خوب و یکی برای مطرح کردن پرسشی که هنوز بی‌جواب مانده است."},"exitItem":{"from":"hr-6-3","kind":"blank","prompt":"What surprised us ___ the fall in absence.","options":["was","were","it was"],"correct":0,"why":{"en":"was: in 'What surprised us was...', the verb is singular and matches the clause. 'Were' is plural, and 'it was' adds an extra subject.","tr":"was: 'What surprised us was...' yapısında fiil tekildir ve yan cümleye uyar. 'Were' çoğuldur; 'it was' fazladan bir özne ekler.","fa":"was درست است، چون در What surprised us was فعل مفرد است و با بند جور است. were جمع است و it was یک فاعل اضافه دارد."}},"expParts":{"hook":{"en":"'What stands out is the drop in late deliveries.' The important part arrives last, when everyone is listening.","tr":"'What stands out is the drop in late deliveries.' Önemli kısım en sonda, herkes dinlerken gelir.","fa":"«⁨What stands out is the drop in late deliveries.⁩» بخش مهم در آخر می‌آید، درست وقتی همه گوش می‌دهند."},"tryWhy":{"en":"is: the wh-clause is one thing, so the verb is is, and nothing else comes before it.","tr":"is: wh- ile başlayan kısım tek bir şeydir; fiil is olur ve önüne başka bir şey gelmez.","fa":"جواب is است: بخش wh یک چیز حساب می‌شود، پس فعل is است و چیز دیگری پیش از آن نمی‌آید."},"rule":[{"en":"What + clause + is/was + the key point.","tr":"What + yan cümle + is/was + asıl nokta.","fa":"الگو این است: What و یک جمله، بعد is یا was و بعد نکته‌ی اصلی.","ex":"What surprised us was the July peak."},{"en":"No it before is.","tr":"is'ten önce it yok.","fa":"پیش از is کلمه‌ی it نمی‌آید.","ex":"What stands out is..., not What stands out it is..."},{"en":"Not 'the thing what': use what alone or the thing that.","tr":"'the thing what' değil: yalnızca what ya da the thing that.","fa":"«the thing what» نه؛ فقط what یا ⁨the thing that⁩.","ex":"What we need to understand is why people leave in summer."}],"test":{"en":"Read up to is. Is that first part a complete 'thing' (what stands out)? Then add nothing before is.","tr":"is'e kadar oku. İlk kısım tam bir 'şey' mi (what stands out)? O zaman is'ten önce hiçbir şey ekleme.","fa":"تا is بخوان. بخش اول یک «چیز» کامل است (what stands out)؟ پس پیش از is چیزی اضافه نکن."},"contrast":{"en":"Persian 'chizi ke jalb-e tavajjoh mikonad, kahesh-e ta'khirhast' and Turkish 'Dikkat çeken şey, ...' work the same way, so the idea is easy. The trap is adding it or writing 'the thing what'.","tr":"Türkçede de aynı yapı vardır: 'Dikkat çeken şey, gecikmelerdeki düşüş.' Tuzak, it eklemek ya da 'the thing what' yazmaktır.","fa":"در فارسی هم همین کار را می‌کنیم: «چیزی که جلب توجه می‌کند، کاهش تأخیرهاست». تله این است که it اضافه کنی یا بنویسی «the thing what»."}},"errorWatch":[{"find":["stands out it is","surprised us it was","the thing what","understand it is"],"fix":{"en":"Use What + clause + is: 'What stands out is the drop in late deliveries.'","tr":"What + yan cümle + is kullan: 'What stands out is the drop in late deliveries.'","fa":"از What و یک جمله و بعد is استفاده کن: «What stands out is the drop in late deliveries.»"}}]},"vocab":{"id":"c-hr-6-3-v","level":"B1","category":"vocab","course":"hr","unit":"hr-6-3","goals":["career"],"title":{"en":"HR Data and Meetings","tr":"İK Verileri ve Toplantılar","fa":"داده‌های منابع انسانی و جلسه"},"cards":[{"word":"turnover","sentence":"Staff turnover in Dubai was 8% this year.","meaning":{"en":"The rate at which people leave and are replaced.","tr":"personel devir hızı.","fa":"نرخ ترک خدمت کارکنان (سرعت رفتن و جایگزین شدن افراد)"}},{"word":"retention","sentence":"Our 90-day retention is 11 out of 12.","meaning":{"en":"Keeping employees; the share who stay.","tr":"çalışanı elde tutma.","fa":"نگهداشت کارکنان (درصد کسانی که می‌مانند)"}},{"word":"headcount","sentence":"Headcount in Dubai rose from 20 to 32.","meaning":{"en":"The number of people employed.","tr":"çalışan sayısı.","fa":"تعداد کارکنان؛ تعداد نیرو"}},{"word":"trend","sentence":"The trend is clearly downward.","meaning":{"en":"The general direction of change.","tr":"eğilim.","fa":"روند (جهت کلی تغییر)"}},{"word":"rise sharply","sentence":"Leavers rose sharply in July.","gap":"rose sharply","accept":["rose sharply","rise sharply"],"meaning":{"en":"To go up quickly and by a lot.","tr":"keskin biçimde artmak.","fa":"به‌شدت و سریع بالا رفتن"}},{"word":"level off","sentence":"After July, turnover levelled off.","gap":"levelled off","accept":["levelled off","leveled off","level off"],"meaning":{"en":"To stop rising or falling and stay steady.","tr":"dengelenmek, sabitlenmek.","fa":"ثابت ماندن (بعد از افزایش یا کاهش)"}},{"word":"peak","sentence":"Turnover peaked in July.","gap":"peaked","accept":["peaked","peak"],"meaning":{"en":"To reach the highest point.","tr":"zirveye ulaşmak.","fa":"به اوج رسیدن"}},{"word":"agenda","sentence":"There are three items on the agenda.","meaning":{"en":"The list of topics for a meeting.","tr":"gündem.","fa":"دستور جلسه"}},{"word":"item","sentence":"The last item is the summer plan.","meaning":{"en":"One topic on a list.","tr":"madde, konu.","fa":"بند؛ یک مورد از فهرست"}},{"word":"define","sentence":"Let me define turnover first.","meaning":{"en":"To say exactly what a word means.","tr":"tanımlamak.","fa":"تعریف کردن (معنی دقیق یک اصطلاح را گفتن)"}}]},"story":{"id":"c-hr-6-3-s","level":"B1","genre":"Workplace","course":"hr","unit":"hr-6-3","title":{"en":"The Numbers","tr":"Rakamlar","fa":"عددها"},"text":"In January, Ms Clarke asked for a short review of the Dubai team before her company renewed its contract. Twenty minutes, on video. Leyla would lead it.\n\nShe started the way she had learned to start everything. \"Thank you for joining. We have three items on the agenda: hiring, turnover and delivery times. We'll finish by half past ten.\"\n\n\"Lovely,\" said Ms Clarke, who said lovely about everything, including bad news.\n\n\"First, hiring. We needed twelve drivers in one quarter, and we hired twelve. Eleven of them are still with us after ninety days.\"\n\n\"Let's move on to turnover.\" She shared a simple line chart. \"Turnover rose sharply in July, when three drivers left in the summer heat. After that it levelled off at about one leaver a month.\"\n\n\"That's interesting,\" said Ms Clarke.\n\nLeyla had worked with Ms Clarke for a year now. That's interesting meant I don't believe you yet.\n\n\"Before I go on,\" Leyla said, \"let me define turnover, so we are reading the chart the same way. It's the number of people who left in a month, divided by the average headcount that month. The data comes from our payroll system, not from managers' estimates.\"\n\n\"Ah,\" said Ms Clarke. This time it sounded like trust.\n\n\"Moving on to delivery times. Late deliveries fell from 9% in March to 3% in December.\"\n\n\"And what will you do about July?\"\n\nIt was the right question. Leyla had the answer ready: earlier shifts in summer and a cooling break every two hours.\n\nAt 10:28 Ms Clarke said, \"Lovely.\" Two days later the contract was renewed for three years.","vocab":[{"word":"review","en":"Here: a meeting to look back at results.","tr":"değerlendirme toplantısı","fa":"جلسه‌ی مرور نتایج"},{"word":"line chart","en":"A graph with a line that shows change over time.","tr":"çizgi grafik","fa":"نمودار خطی"},{"word":"divided by","en":"Split into equal parts by a number.","tr":"... bölü ...","fa":"تقسیم بر"},{"word":"estimate","en":"A guess about a number.","tr":"tahmin","fa":"برآورد؛ تخمین"},{"word":"cooling break","en":"A short rest to cool down in hot weather.","tr":"serinleme molası","fa":"استراحت کوتاه برای خنک شدن در گرما"}],"quiz":[{"prompt":"Why did Leyla define turnover in the middle of the meeting?","options":["She forgot to do it earlier","Ms Clarke's \"That's interesting\" showed she did not trust the numbers yet","It was on the agenda"],"correct":1},{"prompt":"Choose the correct sentence.","options":["Turnover raised sharply in July.","Turnover rised sharply in July.","Turnover rose sharply in July."],"correct":2},{"prompt":"What happened to late deliveries?","options":["They fell from 9% to 3%","They rose sharply","They levelled off at 9%"],"correct":0},{"prompt":"What made Ms Clarke trust the numbers?","options":["The chart had nice colours","Leyla explained the definition and the data source","Leyla spoke quickly"],"correct":1}],"notice":{"en":"Ms Clarke says 'That's interesting' at one point. Leyla knows what it really means. Watch what she does next.","tr":"Ms Clarke bir noktada 'That's interesting' diyor. Leyla bunun gerçekte ne anlama geldiğini biliyor. Ardından ne yaptığına dikkat et.","fa":"خانم کلارک جایی می‌گوید «That's interesting». لیلا می‌داند معنی واقعی‌اش چیست. دقت کن بعدش چه می‌کند."},"bridge":{"en":"'Turnover rose sharply in July, then levelled off.' Next: see the verbs and adverbs of data talk.","tr":"'Turnover rose sharply in July, then levelled off.' Sırada: veri konuşmasının fiillerini ve zarflarını gör.","fa":"«⁨Turnover rose sharply in July, then levelled off.⁩» قدم بعد: فعل‌ها و قیدهای مخصوص حرف زدن درباره‌ی داده را ببین."}},"speaking":{"id":"hr-6-3","course":"hr","unit":"hr-6-3","rounds":[120,90,60],"topic":{"en":"Presenting HR Data to a Client","tr":"Bir Müşteriye İK Verilerini Sunmak","fa":"ارائه‌ی داده‌های منابع انسانی به مشتری"},"warmup":{"en":"Look at any number from your work this month. Did it rise, fall or level off?","tr":"Bu ay işinden herhangi bir sayıya bak. Arttı mı, azaldı mı, sabitlendi mi?","fa":"یک عدد از کار این ماهت را در نظر بگیر. بالا رفت، پایین آمد یا ثابت ماند؟"},"questions":[{"en":"Open the meeting: purpose, three agenda items and the finish time.","tr":"Toplantıyı aç: amaç, üç gündem maddesi ve bitiş saati.","fa":"جلسه را شروع کن: هدف، سه بند دستور جلسه و ساعت پایان."},{"en":"Present two trends with a verb and an adverb each. Signpost between them.","tr":"Her biri bir fiil ve bir zarfla iki eğilim sun. Aralarında geçişi belirt.","fa":"دو روند را توضیح بده، هر کدام با یک فعل و یک قید. میان آن‌ها با یک عبارت انتقالی اعلام کن که موضوع عوض می‌شود."},{"en":"Ms Clarke asks: \"How do you define turnover?\" Answer clearly, then close with one action.","tr":"Ms Clarke soruyor: \"Personel devir hızını nasıl tanımlıyorsunuz?\" Açıkça cevap ver, sonra bir eylemle kapat.","fa":"خانم کلارک می‌پرسد: «⁨How do you define turnover?⁩» روشن جواب بده و بعد جلسه را با یک اقدام مشخص جمع‌بندی کن."}],"followups":[{"en":"Give the 2-minute presentation, then again in 90 seconds, then in 60.","tr":"2 dakikalık sunumu yap, sonra 90 saniyede, sonra 60 saniyede tekrarla.","fa":"ارائه را یک بار در دو دقیقه انجام بده، بعد در ۹۰ ثانیه و بعد در ۶۰ ثانیه."},{"en":"Now describe one real number at your company and how it has changed.","tr":"Şimdi şirketindeki gerçek bir rakamı ve nasıl değiştiğini anlat.","fa":"حالا یک عدد واقعی در شرکتت و تغییرش را توصیف کن."}],"expressions":[{"phrase":"We have three items on the agenda.","meaning":{"en":"Opens the meeting.","tr":"Toplantıyı açar.","fa":"جلسه را شروع می‌کند."}},{"phrase":"Let's move on to...","meaning":{"en":"Changes topic.","tr":"Konuyu değiştirir.","fa":"به موضوع بعدی می‌رود."}},{"phrase":"Let me define..., so we read it the same way.","meaning":{"en":"Builds trust in the numbers.","tr":"Sayılara güven oluşturur.","fa":"اعتماد به عددها را بیشتر می‌کند."}}],"culture":{"en":"Many British speakers use mild words to show doubt or disagreement. \"That's interesting\" or \"I hear what you say\" can mean \"I'm not convinced\". \"With respect\" often comes before a disagreement. When you hear them, slow down and give a definition, a source or an example.","tr":"Birçok İngiliz şüphe ya da itirazı göstermek için yumuşak sözcükler kullanır. \"That's interesting\" ya da \"I hear what you say\" \"ikna olmadım\" anlamına gelebilir. \"With respect\" çoğu zaman bir itirazdan önce gelir. Bunları duyduğunda yavaşla ve bir tanım, kaynak ya da örnek ver.","fa":"بسیاری از بریتانیایی‌ها تردید یا مخالفتشان را با کلمه‌های ملایم نشان می‌دهند. «That's interesting» یا «I hear what you say» ممکن است در واقع یعنی «قانع نشدم». «With respect» هم اغلب درست قبل از یک مخالفت می‌آید. وقتی این عبارت‌ها را می‌شنوی، آهسته‌تر پیش برو و یک تعریف، یک منبع یا یک مثال بیاور."},"model":"Thank you for joining. We have three items on the agenda: hiring, turnover and delivery times. We'll finish by half past ten. First, hiring: we hired twelve drivers, and eleven are still with us. Let's move on to turnover. It rose sharply in July, then levelled off. Let me define turnover, so we read it the same way: leavers divided by average headcount.","selfCheck":[{"en":"I gave the purpose, three agenda items and the finish time.","tr":"Amacı, üç gündem maddesini ve bitiş saatini söyledim.","fa":"هدف، سه موضوع جلسه و ساعت پایان را گفتم."},{"en":"Each trend had a verb and an adverb (rose sharply).","tr":"Her eğilimde bir fiil ve bir zarf vardı (rose sharply).","fa":"هر روند یک فعل و یک قید داشت (rose sharply)."},{"en":"I signposted between topics (Let's move on to...).","tr":"Konular arasında geçişi belirttim (Let's move on to...).","fa":"رفتن به موضوع بعدی را اعلام کردم (⁨Let's move on to...⁩)."},{"en":"I defined one term clearly and closed with an action.","tr":"Bir terimi net tanımladım ve bir eylemle bitirdim.","fa":"یک اصطلاح را روشن تعریف کردم و با یک اقدام تمام کردم."}]},"writing":{"id":"c-hr-6-3-w","title":{"en":"The follow-up to Ms Clarke","tr":"Ms Clarke'a takip e-postası","fa":"ایمیل پیگیری برای خانم کلارک"},"course":"hr","unit":"hr-6-3","type":"writing","difficulty":"medium","prompt":{"en":"Write the follow-up email to Ms Clarke after the review (70-100 words): thank her, give three data points (one rise, one fall, one levelling off), define one term, and state the summer action.","tr":"Değerlendirme toplantısından sonra Ms Clarke'a takip e-postası yaz (70-100 kelime): teşekkür et, üç veri ver (bir artış, bir azalış, bir dengelenme), bir terimi tanımla ve yaz eylemini belirt.","fa":"ایمیل پیگیری بعد از جلسه‌ی مرور نتایج را برای خانم کلارک بنویس (۷۰ تا ۱۰۰ کلمه): از او تشکر کن، سه داده بیاور (یک افزایش، یک کاهش، یک ثابت ماندن)، یک اصطلاح را تعریف کن و اقدامی را که برای تابستان در نظر داری بگو."},"model":"Dear Ms Clarke, Thank you for your time this morning. As promised, here is a short summary. We hired twelve drivers last quarter, and eleven are still with us after ninety days. Turnover rose sharply in July, when three drivers left, and then levelled off at about one leaver a month. We define turnover as leavers divided by average headcount. Late deliveries fell from 9% to 3%. This summer we will start shifts earlier and add a cooling break every two hours. Kind regards, Leyla Karimi","frame":"Dear ___, Thank you for ___. As promised, here is a short summary. ___ rose sharply ___, and then levelled off at ___. We define ___ as ___. ___ fell from ___ to ___. This summer we will ___. Kind regards, ___","words":[{"word":"rose"},{"word":"fell"},{"word":"levelled off"}],"minWords":70,"minSentences":6,"rubric":["Task done: thanks, three trends, one definition, one action","Organised: one data point per sentence, action last","Language: rose / fell / levelled off with adverbs; past simple","Tone: confident and honest; bad news not hidden"],"rubricI18n":{"tr":["Görev: teşekkür, üç eğilim, bir tanım, bir eylem","Düzen: her cümlede bir veri, eylem en sonda","Dil: zarflarla rose / fell / levelled off; past simple","Üslup: kendinden emin ve dürüst; kötü haber gizlenmemiş"],"fa":["کامل بودن کار: تشکر، سه روند، یک تعریف، یک اقدام","نظم: در هر جمله یک داده، اقدام در آخر","زبان: rose / fell / levelled off همراه با قید؛ گذشته‌ی ساده","لحن: مطمئن و صادقانه؛ خبر بد پنهان نشده"]},"portfolio":null,"parts":[{"t":{"en":"Thanks","tr":"Teşekkür","fa":"تشکر"},"find":["thank you"],"sample":"thanks for this morning"},{"t":{"en":"Three trends: a rise, a fall, a levelling off","tr":"Üç eğilim: bir artış, bir düşüş, bir duraklama","fa":"سه روند: یک افزایش، یک کاهش، یک ثابت ماندن"},"find":["rose","fell","levelled off"],"sample":"turnover rose sharply in July, then levelled off; late deliveries fell from 9% to 3%"},{"t":{"en":"One definition","tr":"Bir tanım","fa":"یک تعریف"},"find":["we define","divided by"],"sample":"turnover = leavers divided by average headcount"},{"t":{"en":"The summer action","tr":"Yaz için alınacak önlem","fa":"اقدام تابستان"},"find":["this summer","we will"],"sample":"earlier shifts; a cooling break every two hours"}]},"perspective":{"id":"c-hr-6-3-p","title":{"en":"Ms Clarke deciding","tr":"Karar veren Ms Clarke","fa":"خانم کلارک در حال تصمیم‌گیری"},"course":"hr","unit":"hr-6-3","type":"perspective","minSentences":2,"prompt":{"en":"You are Ms Clarke, deciding whether to renew a three-year contract. Write 2-3 sentences in first person: what made you trust Leyla's numbers, and what would have made you doubt them?","tr":"Üç yıllık bir sözleşmeyi yenileyip yenilememeye karar veren Ms Clarke'sın. Birinci tekil şahısla 2-3 cümle yaz: Leyla'nın rakamlarına güvenmeni ne sağladı ve neyden şüphe ederdin?","fa":"تو خانم کلارک هستی و باید درباره‌ی تمدید یک قرارداد سه‌ساله تصمیم بگیری. از زبان خودت دو یا سه جمله بنویس: چه چیزی باعث شد به عددهای لیلا اعتماد کنی، و چه چیزی ممکن بود تو را به آن‌ها مشکوک کند؟"}},"exit":{"id":"c-hr-6-3-x","course":"hr","unit":"hr-6-3","type":"exit","items":[{"from":"hr-6-3","kind":"blank","prompt":"Absence ___ to 2% in March.","options":["fell","felt","fallen"],"correct":0,"point":2,"why":{"en":"fell: the past of 'fall' is fell. 'Felt' is the past of feel, and 'fallen' needs has or had.","tr":"fell: 'fall' fiilinin geçmişi fell'dir. 'Felt' feel'in geçmişidir; 'fallen' has ya da had ister.","fa":"fell درست است، چون گذشته‌ی fall همان fell است. felt گذشته‌ی feel است و fallen به has یا had نیاز دارد."}},{"from":"hr-6-3","kind":"blank","prompt":"Late deliveries ___ off at around 3%.","options":["levelled","levelling","level"],"correct":0,"point":2,"why":{"en":"levelled: 'levelled off' (past) means stopped rising or falling. 'Levelling' has no be, and 'level' doesn't fit a past trend.","tr":"levelled: 'levelled off' (geçmiş) artmayı ya da düşmeyi durdurmak demektir. 'Levelling'de be yoktur; 'level' geçmişteki bir eğilime uymaz.","fa":"levelled درست است، چون levelled off یعنی دیگر بالا یا پایین نرفت. levelling بدون be است و level با روند گذشته جور نیست."},"hint2":{"en":"This happened in the past, and level off is a regular verb. Which form is the past simple?","tr":"Bu geçmişte oldu ve level off düzenli bir fiil. Geçmiş zaman biçimi hangisi?","fa":"این در گذشته اتفاق افتاده و ⁨level off⁩ یک فعل باقاعده است. شکل گذشته‌ی ساده‌اش کدام است؟"}},{"from":"hr-6-3","kind":"mcq","prompt":"A British client says \"That's interesting\" about your chart. What is the best next step?","options":["Move on quickly","Define your terms and give the data source","Say \"Thank you\""],"correct":1,"point":4,"why":{"en":"Define your terms and give the source: a British 'That's interesting' may be a polite doubt. Moving on or saying thank you leaves the doubt.","tr":"Terimleri tanımla ve kaynağı ver: İngiliz birinin 'That's interesting' demesi kibar bir şüphe olabilir. Geçip gitmek ya da teşekkür etmek şüpheyi bırakır.","fa":"تعریف‌ها و منبع داده را بگو، چون «That's interesting» از زبان یک بریتانیایی ممکن است شکی مؤدبانه باشد. رد شدن یا تشکر کردن آن شک را سر جایش می‌گذارد."}},{"from":"hr-6-2","kind":"blank","prompt":"If you ___ on Monday, we will send your laptop on Friday.","options":["will start","start","would start"],"correct":1,"point":2,"why":{"en":"start: a firm plan takes if + present, then will. 'Will start' and 'would start' can't follow if here.","tr":"start: kesin bir plan if + geniş zaman, sonra will alır. 'Will start' ve 'would start' burada if'ten sonra gelmez.","fa":"start درست است، چون برنامه‌ی قطعی با if و حال ساده و بعد will می‌آید. will start و would start اینجا بعد از if نمی‌آیند."}},{"from":"hr-5-4","kind":"blank","prompt":"He would like ___ a trainer.","options":["to become","becoming","become"],"correct":0,"point":2,"why":{"en":"to become: 'would like' takes to + verb. 'Becoming' and 'become' don't follow would like.","tr":"to become: 'would like' to + fiil alır. 'Becoming' ve 'become' would like'tan sonra gelmez.","fa":"to become درست است، چون would like با to و فعل می‌آید. becoming و become بعد از would like نمی‌آیند."}},{"from":"hr-2-4","kind":"blank","prompt":"Retention in Dubai is ___ than in Istanbul.","options":["more high","higher","highest"],"correct":1,"point":2,"why":{"en":"higher: a short adjective takes -er before than. 'More high' is wrong for a short word, and 'highest' compares three or more.","tr":"higher: kısa sıfat than'den önce -er alır. Kısa kelimede 'more high' yanlıştır; 'highest' üç ve daha fazlasını karşılaştırır.","fa":"⁨higher⁩ درست است، چون صفت کوتاه قبل از ⁨than⁩ ⁨-er⁩ می‌گیرد. ⁨more high⁩ برای کلمه‌ی کوتاه غلط است و ⁨highest⁩ برای سه یا بیشتر است."}}]}}; })(globalThis.COURSE_FILES = globalThis.COURSE_FILES || {});
